Hello everyone, I hope you are all doing well,

March is right around the corner, so here are the dates and times for the O=
rientations that we have planned for March 2025.  First off, we try to have=
 our new arriving Hosts arrive at the State Park on the final day of the cu=
rrent month to get settled in and set up for the big day of Orientations th=
at we hold on the 1st of the new month.  For this month, please try to arri=
ve on the 28th of February to your designated campsite as we will be jumpin=
g into trainings in the morning of the 1st.  If you are unsure of what site=
 you are headed to, please contact me .  We try to hold most of the orienta=
tions on the 1st of the new month so that everyone is all trained up and re=
ady to start their shifts, as some of you will have a shift that starts on =
the 1st of March.

If anyone still needs to complete the required trainings on the Volunteer V=
oice Website, I have placed a link below.  The required trainings are the f=
ollowing: The Park Host Safety Training, The DAS Discrimination and Harassm=
ent Training, and the Volunteer Service Agreement. These trainings must be =
completed annually, so if you have not done them yet for 2025 then please d=
o.

OPRD Volunteer Voice - Forms, Requirements, Resources<https://sites.google.=
com/view/oprdvolunteervoice/forms-requirements-resources>



The Welcome Center Operations Orientation will be held on December 1st at 1=
0am @ the Welcome Center.

The Yurt & Site Maintenance Orientation will be on December 1st at 11am @ t=
he A loop Restroom/Pipe Chase.

The All-Host General Orientation will be at 1pm on March 3rd @ the Welcome =
Center.  For the All-Host General Orientation we ask that all of our curren=
t and new hosts attend so that we can all introduce ourselves to one anothe=
r and also meet the Ranger Staff here at Honeyman State Park as well as tal=
k about upcoming events or trainings that Park Staff will be attending.  If=
 you have your own chair, please bring it as we tend to run out in the welc=
ome center.  Once the meet and greet portion is over, only our new arrivals=
 for March will need to attend the rest of the Orientation.  I will also be=
 giving out gloves, hats, and vests if you are in need of those once the pr=
esentation is over.

I have also attached a copy of the March Schedule for your viewing pleasure=
.




[cid:image001.jpg@01DB879B.DD7E3C80]Logan Bliss | Volunteer Services Lead/R=
anger 1
